--- stderr
factory state: unknown command "jobs"
usage: factory state [--state-dir DIR | --state-url URL] [--json] <command> [flags] [id]

Reads the dispatcher's state directly: no server, no API, no token. Read-only, it
works while factory serve runs, on a copy of the dir, and on the bucket of a --state-url
(gs://, s3:// or file://; its credentials come from the environment, as serve's do).
--state-dir defaults to $FACTORY_STATE_DIR, else ~/.factory/state (deploy/poc/run.sh: ${FACTORY_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.factory/state}).

commands:
  tasks     the tasks: id, spec, phase, reason, work item, created, last run
  task      a task: its spec, status, runs with their results, and the decision that dispatched it
  run       a run: its Result, progress and usage; --transcript prints the transcript (gunzipped)
  workitem  a work item: links, state, counters, decisions and tasks
  events    the events: time, type, source, object, work item, processed
  log       the journal or the log (the changes since the snapshot) as a timeline
  reset     move the state dir aside to <dir>.<UTC time>, for a clean start: open items restart with no state and no run counters (not while a dispatcher has it open; not for --state-url)
